From b0df95c6fc271bd539e780d8ec402385d25f4fa2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mal359 <mal359@icloud.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 19:59:41 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] zero-dimension

ParsePixels: reject zero-dimension XPM images

The existing dimension checks in ParsePixels() reject mismatched
zeros (width==0 with height!=0, or vice versa) but accept the case
where both width and height are zero.

As a result, a 0x0 XPM can therefore pass parsing and reach the function
WritePixels(), which computes the row loop bound as "h = height - 1"
using unsigned arithmetic.

With a zero height this underflows to UINT_MAX, causing a near-infinite
write loop.

To avoid that issue, simply reject any image with a zero width or height
dimension as an invalid XPM file.

Found by AISLE in partnership with Red Hat

AISLE-Report-PSIRTSUPT-14424

CVE-2026-94287

Reported-by: Aisle Research
Assisted-by: AI
Signed-off-by: Olivier Fourdan <ofourdan@redhat.com>
Fixes: 6e42eb9e1 - ParsePixels: reject zero-dimension XPM images
Part-of: <https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/xorg/lib/libxpm/-/merge_requests/33>
---
 libXpm-3.5.19/src/parse.c | 5 +----
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/libXpm-3.5.19/src/parse.c b/libXpm-3.5.19/src/parse.c
index 283e278..1c6265d 100644
--- a/libXpm-3.5.19/src/parse.c
+++ b/libXpm-3.5.19/src/parse.c
@@ -419,10 +419,7 @@ ParsePixels(
     unsigned int a, x, y;
     int ErrorStatus;
 
-    if ((width == 0) && (height != 0))
-	return (XpmFileInvalid);
-
-    if ((height == 0) && (width != 0))
+    if (width == 0 || height == 0)
 	return (XpmFileInvalid);
 
     if ((height > 0 && width >= UINT_MAX / height) ||
